.*
.* QTOCCFG: CFGTCP, the TCP/IP configuration menu, with its related
.* tables menu (option 21) and the point-to-point menu (option 22,
.* CFGTCPPTP). The driver is work/qsjob/src/panels/tcp/; a RETURN
.* option is a list it shows, a CMD option a command it runs.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='CFGTCP'.
:KEYL NAME=MENUKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=CFGTCP HELP=HLPCFG KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.Configure TCP/IP
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='RETURN 101'.Work with TCP/IP interfaces
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='RETURN 102'.Work with TCP/IP routes
:MENUI OPTION=3 ACTION='CMD ?CHGTCPA'.Change TCP/IP attributes
:MENUI OPTION=4 ACTION='RETURN 104'.Work with TCP/IP port restrictions
:MENUI OPTION=10 ACTION='RETURN 110'.Work with TCP/IP host table entries
:MENUI OPTION=11 ACTION='CMD ?MRGTCPHT'.Merge TCP/IP host table
:MENUI OPTION=12 ACTION='CMD ?CHGTCPDMN'.Change TCP/IP domain information
:MENUI OPTION=20 ACTION='CMD CFGTCPAPP'.Configure TCP/IP applications
:MENUI OPTION=21 ACTION='RETURN 121'.Configure related tables
:MENUI OPTION=22 ACTION='CMD CFGTCPPTP'.Configure point-to-point TCP/IP
:MENUI OPTION=23 ACTION='RETURN 123'.Load/Unload IP Filter
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=CFGTBL HELP=HLPTBL KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Configure Related Tables
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD WRKSRVTBLE'.Work with service table entries
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='CMD WRKPCLTBLE'.Work with protocol table entries
:MENUI OPTION=3 ACTION='CMD WRKNETTBLE'.Work with network table entries
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=CFGPTP HELP=HLPPTP KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Configure Point-to-Point TCP/IP
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='RETURN 202'.Work with active point-to-point jobs
:MENUGRP.Modem information options
:MENUI OPTION=11 ACTION='RETURN 211'.Work with modem information
:EMENUGRP.
:MENUGRP.Other related options:
:MENUI OPTION=21 ACTION='RETURN 221'.Work with PPP line descriptions
:MENUI OPTION=22 ACTION='RETURN 222'.Work with PPP line description status
:EMENUGRP.
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPCFG.Configure TCP/IP - Help
:P.Everything TCP/IP uses: the interfaces with their addresses, the routes,
the stack's attributes, the ports kept for chosen user profiles, the host
table, the local names and the name servers, the applications and the
tables of services, protocols and networks.
:P.Type an option number or a command and press Enter. F4 prompts the
command, F9 brings the previous one back, F12 returns to where you were.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPTBL.Configure Related Tables - Help
:P.The services table names the ports of well-known services; the
protocol and network tables name protocols and networks. Programs look
names up in them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPPTP.Configure Point-to-Point TCP/IP - Help
:P.Point-to-point profiles connect over modems and PPP lines, which this
release does not have.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
